d 'XTDYNGCCE': module to provide bootstrap and generalized inference for CCE panel data models
d
d  xtdyngcce provides two estimation commands for panel data models
d with unobserved common factors (interactive fixed effects),
d extending the Common Correlated Effects framework of Pesaran
d (2006) in two directions that are not currently available in
d Stata. xtdyncce fits the pooled CCE estimator in dynamic panels
d and implements the recursive-design wild bootstrap of Juodis,
d Stauskas and Tromp (2026, arXiv:2609.31442). In each replication
d the dependent variable is regenerated recursively and the
d cross-sectional averages are re-estimated from the bootstrap
d data; both steps are required by the theory and distinguish the
d procedure from a residual wild bootstrap. The command also
d provides the three bias corrections benchmarked in that paper --
d the half-panel jackknife of Dhaene and Jochmans (2015), the
d analytical correction of Moon and Weidner (2017), and the fixed-T
d minimum-distance correction of De Vos and Everaert (2021) -- a
d leave-one-out jackknife variance in which the factor estimates
d also omit the deleted unit, and an iterated (double) bootstrap
d for studentized confidence intervals. xtgcce fits the Generalized
d CCE mean-group estimator of Lu, Su and Ba (2026, Journal of
d Econometrics 253, 106183). It augments the regression with the
d time-series averages of the regressors in addition to the usual
d cross-sectional averages. The time-series averages act as control
d variables for the factor loadings, which makes the estimator
d doubly robust: consistent under either the usual CCE rank
d condition or the paper's control-variable condition, with no
d efficiency loss when the rank condition holds. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: pooled CCE
d KW: generalized CCE
d KW: mean-group estimator
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261018
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f xtdyncce.ado
f xtdyncce.sthlp
f xtdyngcce_example.do
f xtdyngcce_mata.ado
f xtdyngcce_methods.sthlp
f xtdyngcce.sthlp
